# armour/man/lamellar: lamellar on the man (LADDER-ARMOUR, STYLE_P2 25.2 / 25.3 / 27.4: the Jade T3, the finer cut of padded
# and leather): vertical 1x3 plates (lit plate pixels step 3, the seams between them a step down) laced by an accent
# line every third row (the cord: accent 2 lit, 1 in shadow); a steel gorget, a belt, a solid band hem.
# Medium weight: the civilian silhouette plus the mid skirt (lamellar_hang, scallops and tassels by `when`) and the shoulders (shared/pauldron_scale*).
# Finish regions: R the gorget's rim and the hem band, P the lit chest, G the chest socket, N the lowest lacing row, W a 2x2
# spot on the shadow side. Keys: rest idle run runl drawn swing lie in D U R L.
# Format: rpg/art/doll/doll.h. Source: LADDER-ARMOUR's expand.py (fill: lamellar).
# (LADDER-ARMOUR polish i1, P5) the lacing courses solid cords, the plate courses smooth planes (the blind
# panel: "the red-dotted lamellar is noise").
# (LADDER-ARMOUR polish i2) only the cord under the gorget and the cord under the belt stay; the middle courses are plate, one big lit plane (the style lens: thin stripes look busy)
# (LADDER-ARMOUR polish i3) quieter: one lacing cord across the chest; below the belt plain lacquer (the panel: "red-dotted
# lamellar is noise", "a stack of orange bars").
# (LADDER-ARMOUR alloys i1) the lamellar in laced lame ROWS: each row a lit top (a step-4 glint on its first lame)
# over a dark underside, the terminator hard (3 to 1): a smooth 3-2-1 gradient read as cloth in any coloured alloy.
# (LADDER-ARMOUR alloys i1) a step-4 specular on the lit top of the first scales / lames / plates (top-left light):
# with no step 4 a coloured alloy read as clay; the glint and the dark core make any metal read as metal.
# (LADDER-ARMOUR alloys i2) the N lacing row dropped from the regions (the style lens: "Jade's lamellar is the busiest
# culture, 1 px gold banding on the torso and legs"): the gorget rim, the belt and the hem carry the trim; the lames
# read by their lit tops and dark undersides alone.
# (LADDER-ARMOUR alloys i3) the chest lames three rows tall (a lit top with its glint, a mid row, a dark underside)
# instead of lit / dark every row (the style lens: "alternating 1 px bands read as striped noise, not plates").
use person
body man
role armour lamellar
layer torso
anchor neck
keys torso
z 2

# >>> BODY envelope fix round 1: brass lamellar (D58) >>>
# A brass or bronze everyday alloy's lamellar coat (D58): rows of small plates in 2 px bands (a hard lit top over a dark
# row), black lacing gaps every 4 px, the right-hand plates a step down; painted in the alloy's brass by the compositor.
# Written by BODY tools/brassrows.py from the `sheen-dark,alloyshape` views (envelope fix round 1); re-run, never hand-edit.
